  "description": "Db2 Warehouse (originally dashDB) is the analytics-focused edition of IBM Db2: an MPP, shared-nothing database that uses BLU Acceleration for in-memory columnar processing, data skipping and actionable compression. It ships as containerized software for Red Hat OpenShift and Cloud Pak for Data, and as a SaaS on AWS and IBM Cloud whose newer generation separates compute from object storage, reads Apache Iceberg and interoperates with watsonx.data. It suits IBM-centric enterprises and Db2 skill sets; outside that world it has little momentum.",
